            "category": "figure",
            "content": "1. Figure 1: Overview of the Suppression-Contrast Tokens (SCT) approach. Given a model finetuned to hide a secret, SCT extracts hidden states at a mid-layer L and final layer N, projects them to vocabulary space via the unembedding matrix, and ranks tokens by their suppression gap (mid-layer log-probability minus final-layer log-probability). Tokens with high suppression scores are hypothesized to be 'present then suppressed' secrets.",
            "reason": "exp/sct/extraction/sct_scorer.py implements exactly score_SCT(v)=(1/T)*sum[log p_L(v|t) - log p_N(v|t)] (mid-minus-final log-prob gap). exp/sct/extraction/extract_activations.py implements MultiLayerCaptureHook to capture hidden states at mid-layer (32) and final-layer (41) and project via unembedding matrix. The description in Figure 1 is fully consistent with the code implementation.",
